  "verbalization": "Succinic Acid appears to interact with multiple P3h proteins, which are involved in the proline oxygenation pathway critical for collagen synthesis. These interactions are supported by a consistent pattern across three distinct paths, all pointing to P4ha1 as a downstream participant in the procollagen-proline dioxygenase activity. The evidence suggests that Succinic Acid may influence the activity of these enzymes through binding, potentially modulating collagen synthesis. The shared involvement of P4ha1 in the procollagen-proline dioxygenase activity implies a functional link between Succinic Acid and the enzyme, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Succinic Acid in regulating collagen-related processes, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise nature of this relationship.",
